tier: opus
branch: feat/work-gateway-wire
depends_on:
owns: src/charon/api.py   # PROVISIONAL — likely also engine/scheduler.py + the coordinator runner; finalize at activation
prompt: (authored on activation)
priority: HIGH — the keystone of the AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER cluster (operator goal 2026-06-27).
scope: AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER (cluster 1/3). `charon work` does NOT route the dispatched agent
  through Charon's own failover gateway, so "point Charon at a non-Claude model and have it work
  tickets" is NOT actually true today. VERIFIED ON origin/master 2026-06-27:
    - The per-run gateway + tier-routing wiring lives ONLY in `api.run_task` (the `charon run
      --role` path): when `role` is set, `run_task` stands up a per-run `GatewayProxyServer`
      (api.py:165/181/340-343), serves a tier-vid pool, and builds the ACP backend through
      `render()` which FORCES `_acp_passthrough_env(include_keys=False)` (api.py:300-307,
      `_acp_via_renderer`) so the agent talks to the loopback gateway, never the provider direct,
      and cost/failover is captured in `proxy_server.status_snapshot()`.
    - The `work` path does NONE of this. `charon work` → `run_work` (cli.py:822) builds a
      `CoordinatorRunner` with `_default_backend_factory(backend_name, acp_cmd)` (cli.py:792),
      whose factory calls `api._resolve_backends(None, None, backend_name, checks, acp_cmd)` —
      NO role, NO tier, NO proxy_server, NO observer, NO renderer.
    - `_resolve_backends` (api.py:355) for the `acp` backend builds a PLAIN
      `AcpBackend(shlex.split(acp_cmd), …, passthrough_env=_acp_passthrough_env())` (api.py:374-375),
      and `_acp_passthrough_env` DEFAULTS to `include_keys=True` (ports/agent_launch.py:38) — its
      own docstring says "The no-proxy interim path still passes keys." So under `charon work`,
      opencode (or any ACP agent) gets the REAL provider keys and talks DIRECTLY to its own
      provider. No Charon gateway in the loop → NO failover, NO tier routing, NO cost capture.
  FIX: thread tier/role + the per-run gateway (GatewayProxyServer) + observer into
  `run_work` / `CoordinatorRunner` / the backend factory so each unit's ACP agent is launched via
  `render()` against the loopback gateway (`include_keys=False`), the same way `run_task --role`
  already does — so ticket work PROVABLY routes through Charon's failover gateway and per-unit cost
  is captured in the ledger. This is THE gap that makes "Charon points a non-Claude model at real
  tickets" actually true end-to-end.
  CONSTRAINTS: agent/provider-agnostic (no opencode/provider hardcode — drive any ACP agent + any
  provider via the gateway); product-clean (no SLOP/fleet/rig leak); stdlib-only privileged core;
  do NOT auto-merge or weaken any propose-default gate; reuse the existing `run_task` gateway/render
  machinery, do NOT fork a second dispatch path (D008 — single fenced coordinator).
note: PARKED. Part of the AUTONOMOUS-TICKET-RUNNER cluster (operator goal 2026-06-27: run real
  tickets via a non-Claude agent through `charon work`). Closing all three (WORK-GATEWAY-WIRE +
  WORK-AGENT-BEARINGS + WORK-LAND-PR), plus WORK-OBSERVABILITY for watching it, makes it
  trustworthy end-to-end. THIS ticket is the keystone: without it, `charon work` never touches
  Charon's gateway at all. Activate when the autonomous-runner goal is prioritized.

